{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>How</b> — the sense: they came to an end, they vanished, upon their lives." "<b>Terrors</b> — like בלהות אתנך (Job 39:20), for there is that which returns to nothingness and to vanity; the proof is ואינך. Like a dream, in which there is no truth upon the dreamer's waking — so their image will be despised in the city. And the sense: they were forgotten, for their memory is forgotten."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:16.500054268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}